  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485), evidence is extremely sparse and the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries independent predictive signal. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is a clean, single-axis comparison to config_001 that isolates modality: it keeps the same profile setting and simplicity level (no aggregation, no fusion) while swapping RNA for image. If image_only performs comparably or better, it validates pursuing multimodal fusion; if it performs poorly, it signals that image adds little and we should focus budget on RNA encoder or profile improvements. Answering this foundational question before investing in any multimodal or multiprofile configuration maximizes information per experiment and prevents misattributing performance gains/losses in later fusion experiments."
}

